\ ring.ga - a token passed around a ring of 36 nodes, rows 0 and 1, for
\ port transfers between many nodes: east along row 0 and west along row 1,
\ 100000 times, adding 1 at node 000 each time, then the low byte of the
\ count on the console. Written by a script: an even column's west port is
\ left and its east right, an odd column's the other way round, and rows 0
\ and 1 share down.

node 000
: main
    right b! down a!
    0 99 for 999 for !b @ 1 + next next
    up b! !b
    left b! @b

node 001
: main right a! left b! begin @ !b again

node 002
: main left a! right b! begin @ !b again

node 003
: main right a! left b! begin @ !b again

node 004
: main left a! right b! begin @ !b again

node 005
: main right a! left b! begin @ !b again

node 006
: main left a! right b! begin @ !b again

node 007
: main right a! left b! begin @ !b again

